   "daf": "84b",
   "sentenceId": 7,
   "he": "כֵּיצַד יַעֲשֶׂה – יִטְּלֶנּוּ הֵימֶנָּה וְכוּ׳: מַאן תַּנָּא? אָמַר חִזְקִיָּה: רַבִּי שִׁמְעוֹן בֶּן אֶלְעָזָר הִיא.",
   "en": "§ It is stated in the mishna: «What should he do» after giving her the bill of divorce and stipulating that she is not permitted to so-and-so? «He should take it from her,» and hand it to her again, and say to her: You are hereby permitted to marry any man. The Gemara asks: «Who» is the tanna who «taught» that? «Ḥizkiyya said» that «it is Rabbi Shimon ben Elazar.»"
  }
